# BUG-608 control: what the refusal leaves alone. A range loop's variable is a counter and
# stays assignable (it steers the loop); a body that re-declares the name binds a new
# local; the name is free again after the loop; and a sibling local is untouched.

def main()
    var out = StringBuilder()
    for i in 0.to(5)
        i = i + 1
        out.append("${i}")
    var xs = [10, 20]
    for x in xs
        var y = x
        y = y + 1
        out.append(" ${y}")
    var x = 0
    x = 7
    out.append(" ${x}")
    print("bug608: ${out.toString()}")
